        <mxCell id="76" parent="Ipro29YhnqW2fJcVF_dH-5" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=40;fontFamily=Architects Daughter;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DArchitects%2BDaughter;" value="On-Premises Data Gateway &#xa;&#xa;&#xa;A Windows Server VM you run on-premises (or in Azure) with Microsoft&#39;s gateway software installed. It&#39;s the only way to connect&#xa;Fabric to on-premises data sources like SQL Server, Oracle, SAP, or file shares.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;How it connects — NO VPN or ExpressRoute needed:&#xa;&#xa;&#xa; Fabric&#xa;    ↕  Azure Service Bus (public internet relay)&#xa; On-Prem Gateway VM&#xa;    ↕  your internal network&#xa; SQL Server / Oracle / File Share&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;The gateway was specifically designed to work in locked-down environments where you can&#39;t set up VPN — as long as the VM can reach&#xa;the internet on port 443, it works." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1500" width="2060" x="3210" y="2190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
